Save a public Notion page, and every page it links to,
as self-contained HTML files that work offline.


    $ uv run notionsnapshot.py https://sueszli.notion.site/NotionSnapshot-Test-tiny-page-4dfa05657f774b45993542da4a8530c2
    $ open snapshot/index.html


Each page becomes one file. Stylesheets, fonts, images,
video and audio are embedded, Notion's JavaScript is removed
and links between pages point at the other local files.
Toggles are saved expanded.

The first run downloads a headless Chromium through
Playwright. The browser cache lives in ~/.cache/notionsnapshot
because Notion rate limits clients that refetch its assets.

Not supported: file attachments, iframe embeds such as
YouTube or Google Maps (they need the network) and
horizontal scrolling in wide database views.
